# The Settings app escalates anyone with push access to admin, because pushing
# .github/settings.yml to the default branch changes repository settings.
# Code-owner review on that file is the mitigation its own docs prescribe.
#
# NOT CURRENTLY ENFORCED: enforcing it needs require_code_owner_reviews in
# settings.yml, which needs an approval requirement, which would deadlock a
# repo with one admin and no other collaborators. This file records the intent
# and takes effect the moment a second collaborator makes the escalation real.
/.github/settings.yml @mchelen
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @mchelen
